.TH XNEC2C "1" "July 2026" "@PACKAGE_STRING@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xnec2c \- a GTK+ graphical interactive version of nec2c,
a translation to C of the FORTRAN application NEC2
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.B xnec2c [\-bcCdijhqvPV]
\fI\,<input-file-name>\/\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PD 0
.IP
\-i|\-\-input         <input\-file\-name>
\-c|\-\-config        <config\-file\-path>     \- file must exist
\-C|\-\-new\-config    <new\-config\-file\-path> \- creates the file when missing
.IP
\-j|\-\-jobs  <number of processors in SMP machine> (-j0 disables forking)
.IP
   \-\-openblas\-threads <n>  set OpenBLAS thread count (default: 1)
.IP
   \-\-mkl\-threads <n>       set Intel MKL thread count (default: 1)
.IP
   \-\-omp\-threads <n>       set OpenMP thread count (default: 1)
.IP
\-b|\-\-batch:        enable batch mode, exit after the frequency loop runs
.IP
\-P|\-\-no\-pthreads:  disable pthreads and use the GTK loop for debugging
.IP
\-h|\-\-help:         print usage information and exit
.IP
\-V|\-\-version:      print xnec2c version number and exit
.IP
\-v|\-\-verbose:      increase verbosity, can be specified multiple times
.IP
\-d|\-\-debug:        enable debug output (-dd includes backtraces)
.IP
\-q|\-\-quiet:        suppress debug/verbose output
.IP
\-\-optimize:         Activate the optimizer immediately.
.IP
\-\-skip\-verify      skip geometry verification checks
.IP
\-\-force\-verify     force overlap check on large models (models with more than 1000 segments)
.IP
\-\-mem\-report       report managed allocator live bytes per call site after each optimizer evaluation
.PP
.sp 2

The following arguments write to an output file after the frequency loop completes.
These are useful to combine with \-\-batch; If you wish to specify filenames to write
without \-\-batch mode then enable the File\->Optimizer Settings or the files you
specify on the command line will not be written.

.sp 2
.IP
\-\-write\-csv             <filename>  \- write CSV file of measurements
.IP
\-\-write\-s1p             <filename>  \- write S1P file of S\-parameters
.IP
\-\-write\-s2p\-max\-gain    <filename>  \- write S2P file, port\-2 is max\-gain
.IP
\-\-write\-s2p\-viewer\-gain <filename>  \- write S2P file, port\-2 is viewer\-gain
.IP
\-\-write\-rdpat           <filename>  \- write CSV of the radiation pattern
.IP
\-\-write\-currents        <filename>  \- write CSV of currents and charges
.IP
\-\-write\-gnuplot\-structure <filename>  \- write gnuplot structure file
.IP
\-\-write\-patch\-currents   <filename>  \- write CSV of patch surface currents
.IP
\-\-write\-validation\-dir  <directory> \- write full validation data tree
.IP
\-\-write\-rdpat\-png       <filename>  \- write PNG of the radiation pattern at the configured saved frequency (see \-\-freq\-select)
.IP
\-\-rdpat\-png\-format     <format[,format...]>  \- select x, y, z, iso, or quad views; defaults to iso. One format preserves <filename>; multiple formats write <filename>\-<format>.png
.IP
\-\-freq\-select <min\-vswr|center|max\-gain|MHz>  \- select the frequency positioned after each sweep: minimum SWR, sweep center, maximum gain, or the computed step nearest the given MHz; absent, the previous saved frequency is kept, or the sweep center when none is available. This selection also drives the \-\-write\-rdpat\-png capture step
.IP
.SH "ENVIRONMENT"
.TP
.B LANGUAGE
Override the system locale for message translation.
For example,
.B LANGUAGE=de xnec2c
selects German.
.TP
.B XNEC2C_LOCALEDIR
Override the compiled-in locale directory.
Set this to the directory containing the
.I LC_MESSAGES
trees when the default path does not match your installation.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
Full documentation is available at the official website for xnec2c
.URL "https://www.xnec2c.org/" "Official xnec2c Website" .
In addition, the full documentation for
.B xnec2c
is maintained as an html document.  If the
.B xnec2c
program is properly installed at your site, a command like
.PD 1
.IP
.B firefox /usr/share/doc/xnec2c/xnec2c.html
.PP
should give you access to the complete manual.
